{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# 🌳 Decision Trees\n**\"Which thing do I use here?\"** — six recurring choices, each with the reason attached.\n\nThese are the questions interviews ask and tutorials skip.","x":-1100,"y":-720,"width":800,"height":160},
		{"id":"g1","type":"group","label":"Which view class?","x":-1140,"y":-520,"width":1000,"height":620},
		{"id":"v0","type":"text","text":"## 🪜 Which view class?","x":-1100,"y":-450,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"v1","type":"text","text":"**Standard CRUD on a model?**\n→ `ModelViewSet` + `DefaultRouter`\n\nFive actions, one class, one line of `urls.py`.","x":-1100,"y":-370,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"v2","type":"text","text":"**Want some actions, not all?**\n→ mixins + `GenericViewSet`\n\nTags: List + Update + Destroy, **no Create** — tags are born inside recipes.","x":-620,"y":-370,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"v3","type":"text","text":"**One collection or one detail URL?**\n→ `ListCreateAPIView`\n→ `RetrieveUpdateDestroyAPIView`\n\nNo router needed.","x":-1100,"y":-210,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"v4","type":"text","text":"**One odd endpoint?**\n→ `APIView`\n\n`/token/`, `/export/`, a webhook receiver. Forcing these into a ViewSet costs more than it saves.","x":-620,"y":-210,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"v5","type":"text","text":"### The rule\nClimb the abstraction ladder only as high as you need. **Every rung above buys less code and costs control.**\n\nWhen the framework's shape stops matching your problem, step down a rung — don't fight it.","x":-1100,"y":-50,"width":920,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"g2","type":"group","label":"Which auth?","x":-100,"y":-520,"width":1000,"height":620},
		{"id":"a0","type":"text","text":"## 🔑 Which auth scheme?","x":-60,"y":-450,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a1","type":"text","text":"**Browser app on the same domain?**\n→ **Session**\n\n`httpOnly` `Secure` `SameSite` cookie — the most XSS-resistant option. The browser manages it.","x":-60,"y":-370,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a2","type":"text","text":"**Mobile / SPA / cross-origin, one backend?**\n→ **DRF Token** + an expiry class\n\nOne indexed PK lookup per request. Revoke by deleting the row.","x":420,"y":-370,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a3","type":"text","text":"**Many services verifying the same identity?**\n→ **JWT**\n\nStateless verification is genuinely worth something here — and only here.","x":-60,"y":-210,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a4","type":"text","text":"### ⚠️ The JWT trap\nYou **cannot revoke** a JWT before it expires. Adding a denylist to fix that puts the database lookup straight back — the only thing JWT bought you.\n\n\"It's the standard\" is not a reason.","x":420,"y":-210,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a5","type":"text","text":"### Storage, whichever you pick\niOS → **Keychain** · Android → **Keystore** · Web → **`httpOnly` cookie**\n\n❌ Never `localStorage` — any injected script, or any compromised npm package, reads it.","x":-60,"y":-50,"width":920,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"g3","type":"group","label":"Why is it slow?","x":-1140,"y":160,"width":1000,"height":540},
		{"id":"s0","type":"text","text":"## 🐌 Why is it slow?","x":-1100,"y":230,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"s1","type":"text","text":"**Step 1 — count the queries**\n\n```python\nwith self.assertNumQueries(4):\n    self.client.get(RECIPES_URL)\n```","x":-1100,"y":310,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"s2","type":"text","text":"**Does the count grow with the rows?**\n→ **N+1.** Fix it:\n\n```python\n.select_related(\"user\")\n.prefetch_related(\"tags\", \"ingredients\")\n```","x":-620,"y":310,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s3","type":"text","text":"**Few queries, still slow?**\n→ **Missing index.** Add one on exactly what you filter and order by:\n\n```python\nindexes = [models.Index(fields=[\"user\", \"-id\"])]\n```","x":-1100,"y":470,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s4","type":"text","text":"**Big response?**\n→ **Paginate.** Then check `?page=5000` — offset pagination makes Postgres fetch and discard 49,990 rows.","x":-620,"y":470,"width":440,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"s5","type":"text","text":"### Cache **last**\nCaching a slow query hides the problem instead of fixing it — and adds an invalidation bug you now own. Fix N+1 and indexes first.","x":-1100,"y":630,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"g4","type":"group","label":"Signal or direct call?","x":-100,"y":160,"width":1000,"height":300},
		{"id":"g0","type":"text","text":"## 📡 Signal or direct call?","x":-60,"y":230,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sg1","type":"text","text":"**Do you own the code that fires the event?**\n\n→ **Yes: just call the function.**\nExplicit beats invisible. The reader sees it on the next line.","x":-60,"y":310,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sg2","type":"text","text":"**→ No: use a signal.**\nYou can't edit `django.contrib.auth`'s `User.save()`, but you can listen to it.\n\n⚠️ Signals don't fire on `bulk_create` or `QuerySet.update()`.","x":420,"y":310,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"g5","type":"group","label":"Sync or background?","x":-1140,"y":760,"width":1000,"height":300},
		{"id":"b0","type":"text","text":"## ⚙️ Sync or background?","x":-1100,"y":830,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"**Does it touch anything outside your database?**\nEmail, third-party API, image processing, PDF generation\n\n→ **Background it.** A worker waiting is not a worker serving.","x":-1100,"y":910,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"### ⚠️ And always `on_commit`\n\n```python\ntransaction.on_commit(\n    lambda: task.delay(obj.id)\n)\n```\n\nOtherwise the worker starts before the row is committed → intermittent `DoesNotExist`.","x":-620,"y":910,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"g6","type":"group","label":"403 or 404?","x":-100,"y":520,"width":1000,"height":300},
		{"id":"c0","type":"text","text":"## 🔢 403 or 404 for someone else's object?","x":-60,"y":590,"width":920,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c1","type":"text","text":"**→ 404, via `get_queryset()` filtering.**\n\n```python\ndef get_queryset(self):\n    return self.queryset.filter(\n        user=self.request.user)\n```","x":-60,"y":670,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c2","type":"text","text":"**Why not 403?**\nA 403 *confirms the object exists*. With sequential IDs an attacker walks the range and maps your database from the status codes alone.\n\n404 leaks nothing.","x":420,"y":670,"width":440,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ref1","type":"file","file":"18.Reference/3.ViewSet and Router Cheatsheet.md","x":-1140,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"ref2","type":"file","file":"17.Production DRF/6.Token vs JWT vs Session.md","x":-640,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"ref3","type":"file","file":"17.Production DRF/4.The N+1 Problem.md","x":-140,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"ref4","type":"file","file":"17.Production DRF/5.Custom Permissions.md","x":360,"y":1100,"width":460,"height":90}
	],
